      },
      "displayName": "scossu",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5fca89b631795a006fe46d8b",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>This seems to be a solid case of predicate filtering in the indexer. I would evaluate the option to broaden the scope to a configurable list of properties that are to be omitted from all indexed resources. </p>\n\n<p>This way, if one really wants ldp:contains triples or someone else has a problem with another predicate, they can accommodate these needs without changing the code. </p>",
